---
title: Form-wide errors and linked summaries
description: Surface root-level validation errors in a polite live-region summary whose links move focus to the offending control only on explicit activation.
---

<script>
	import { Callout } from "$lib/markdown";
</script>

Some errors belong to no single field — "the end date must be after the start date" is about the booking, not about either date input. Superforms collects every error in `$allErrors`, including root errors under `_errors`. Render them in one summary region with links to the controls that have a target, and readable text for those that do not.

## Produce a root error in the schema

A `superRefine` issue without a `path` lands in `$errors._errors`:

```ts title="src/routes/bookings/schema.ts"
import { z } from "zod/v3";

export const bookingSchema = z
	.object({
		start: z.string().min(1, "Choose a start date."),
		end: z.string().min(1, "Choose an end date."),
		contactNeeded: z.boolean().default(false),
		phone: z.string().default(""),
	})
	.superRefine((booking, context) => {
		if (booking.contactNeeded && !booking.phone.trim()) {
			context.addIssue({
				code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,
				path: ["phone"],
				message: "Enter a contact phone number.",
			});
		}
		const start = Date.parse(booking.start);
		const end = Date.parse(booking.end);
		if (!Number.isNaN(start) && !Number.isNaN(end) && end <= start) {
			// No field path: Superforms puts this cross-field issue in errors._errors.
			context.addIssue({
				code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,
				message: "The end date must be after the start date.",
			});
		}
	});

export type BookingData = z.infer<typeof bookingSchema>;
```

The worked example validates real calendar dates before comparing year, month and day components; impossible dates become field errors on `start` or `end`.

## Give each form its own ID and action

```ts title="src/routes/bookings/+page.server.ts"
import { fail } from "@sveltejs/kit";
import { message, superValidate } from "sveltekit-superforms";
import { zod } from "sveltekit-superforms/adapters";
import { bookingSchema } from "./schema.js";

export const load = async () => ({
	personal: await superValidate(zod(bookingSchema), { id: "booking-personal" }),
	work: await superValidate(zod(bookingSchema), { id: "booking-work" }),
});

async function save(request: Request, id: string) {
	const form = await superValidate(request, zod(bookingSchema), { id });
	if (!form.valid) return fail(400, { form });
	return message(form, "Booking saved.");
}

export const actions = {
	personal: ({ request }) => save(request, "booking-personal"),
	work: ({ request }) => save(request, "booking-work"),
};
```

## Render the summary

The form component maps known paths to readable labels, explicit `Control` IDs and bound input refs. Root and unmapped errors stay readable text — never link them to an arbitrary control. The summary region stays mounted, even while empty:

```svelte title="src/routes/bookings/booking-form.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { tick, untrack } from "svelte";
	import { superForm, type SuperValidated } from "sveltekit-superforms";
	import { Control, Field, Label } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
	import type { BookingData } from "./schema.js";

	let { validated }: { validated: SuperValidated<BookingData> } = $props();

	const prefix = "booking-personal";
	const form = superForm(untrack(() => validated), {
		id: prefix,
		resetForm: false,
		// Clear through Superforms so an identical rejection restores fresh summary
		// content inside the same live region.
		clearOnSubmit: "errors",
		// The summary is the sole announcement; links move focus only on request.
		autoFocusOnError: false,
		scrollToError: "off",
	});
	const { form: formData, errors, allErrors, enhance, message } = form;

	let startInput = $state<HTMLInputElement>();

	const labels: Record<string, string> = { start: "Start date" };
	const targets = $derived({ start: { id: `${prefix}-start`, element: startInput } });

	function targetFor(path: string) {
		return path === "start" ? targets[path] : undefined;
	}

	async function focusTarget(event: MouseEvent, path: string) {
		event.preventDefault();
		await tick();
		targetFor(path)?.element?.focus();
	}
</script>

<form method="POST" action="?/personal" use:enhance novalidate>
	<!-- Keep one polite, atomic live region mounted, including while empty. -->
	<div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
		{#if $allErrors.length}
			<section aria-labelledby={`${prefix}-summary-title`}>
				<h3 id={`${prefix}-summary-title`}>Check this booking</h3>
				<ul>
					{#each $allErrors as error (error.path)}
						{@const target = targetFor(error.path)}
						{#each error.messages as errorMessage, index (index)}
							<li>
								{#if target}
									<a
										href={`#${target.id}`}
										onclick={(event) => focusTarget(event, error.path)}
										>{labels[error.path]}: {errorMessage}</a
									>
								{:else}
									{labels[error.path] ?? "Booking"}: {errorMessage}
								{/if}
							</li>
						{/each}
					{/each}
				</ul>
			</section>
		{/if}
	</div>

	<!-- novalidate makes the server schema responsible for native POSTs too. -->
	<Field {form} name="start" fieldErrors fieldErrorsLive="off">
		<Control id={`${prefix}-start`}>
			{#snippet children({ props })}
				<Label>{labels.start}</Label>
				<input {...props} type="date" bind:value={$formData.start} bind:this={startInput} />
			{/snippet}
		</Control>
	</Field>

	<button type="submit">Save booking</button>
	<!-- Clearing uses Superforms' error store, without changing values or focus. -->
	<button type="button" onclick={() => errors.set({}, { force: true })}>Clear errors</button>
	{#if $message}<p>{$message}</p>{/if}
</form>
```

## How it works

- `fieldErrorsLive="off"` keeps each field's error association without repeating the announcement — the summary is the only live region.
- Caller-owned IDs are supplied to `Control` and used directly in `href`s. Never derive target IDs from field paths or from Formsnap-generated IDs.
- `clearOnSubmit: "errors"` clears the previous summary through Superforms while the request is pending; values and any other form's errors are unchanged.
- `autoFocusOnError: false` and `scrollToError: "off"` stop Superforms from competing with your links for focus on rejection. This is a per-form policy, not a Formsnap default.
- If a link's target can disappear (a conditional section, for example), re-read the mapping after `tick()` before focusing so a removed section cannot leave a stale reference — and keep the readable error text as the fallback.

<Callout type="warning">

A successful submission re-runs the route's `load`, and every form whose ID appears in the refreshed data rebinds to it, dropping that form's values and errors. With two booking forms on one page, submitting one can re-initialize the other — return the saved record from `load`, or set Superforms' `invalidateAll: false` on the form that must not refresh.

</Callout>
